WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:05.150
- [Narrator] Welcome to New York City.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.100
The crown jewel of the real estate market.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.650
Everybody wants a piece.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.080
And now, thanks to blockchain technology,

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.440
that may very well be possible.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.590
This $36.5 million development

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:19.890
is being sliced into digital shares,

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.610
or tokenized, as it's called,

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.059
so that investors around the world

00:00:23.059 --> 00:00:26.420
can own as much, or as
little, as they can afford.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.899
- We have the typical bank
financing on this project

00:00:28.899 --> 00:00:33.540
with a conventional bank, and
this loan matures in January.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:36.370
We've decided to take a right turn

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.623
and tokenize the debt
here on the property.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:42.517
The construction is 95% complete,

00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:46.210
we are starting to get inspections
in the next week or so.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.917
- We have a bank deadline on us,

00:00:47.917 --> 00:00:50.150
where we have to sell a
certain amount of units

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.050
or repay the entire
loan by a certain date.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.530
If construction's been delayed,

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.320
if the market turns,
if competition pops up,

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.850
and we're not going to be
able to hit that deadline,

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.220
what do you do?

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:01.940
So by tokenizing the debt,

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.050
it gives everyone breathing room

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:08.290
to sell at a normal pace with the market

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:09.643
instead of against it.

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.310
- [Narrator] The people
behind this offering

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:15.680
reside across the East
River, in that other borough.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.040
Here, the blockchain start-up, Fluidity,

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.630
has teamed up with
broker-dealer firm, Propellor,

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:23.770
to generate tokens by
crafting smart contracts,

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.050
and in so doing, they
could be changing the way

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:28.340
we all do business in the future.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.320
- When we started to look
at the real estate industry,

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.182
it's probably one of the
most inefficient industries

00:01:32.182 --> 00:01:34.270
that exist currently.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:35.590
You have a lot of
middlemen, a lot of lawyers,

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:37.703
a lot of bankers and
just being able to create

00:01:37.703 --> 00:01:41.970
something that has real impact
on an industry like that,

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.950
I think you're looking at
significant disruption.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.290
- [Narrator] But for a project determined

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:49.300
to eliminate middlemen, there's
a lot of people involved.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.430
- Motivator.
- Coder.

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:51.700
- I'm a lawyer.
- Facilitator.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:52.864
- Strategy.
- Project Manager.

00:01:52.864 --> 00:01:54.155
- Developer.
- Co-founder.

00:01:54.155 --> 00:01:55.470
- I'm just the broker.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:56.303
- I'm a fan.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.670
- [Narrator] An important
party that is absent

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.590
in this equation is a bank.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:02.490
- There will not be a bank involved.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.240
- [Narrator] The process
goes something like this.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.430
These guys create tokens
on the blockchain.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:08.810
The tokens represent
the condo unit's debt,

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.420
and can be traded as private securities.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:13.250
If token holders sell their shares,

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.010
the purchaser can either
preserve the tokens

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.310
on the blockchain, or cash them out,

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.630
thereby dissolving
these tokens altogether.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:22.304
This, theoretically, would
produce more liquidity

00:02:22.304 --> 00:02:25.130
to a notoriously ill-liquid market.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:27.340
- It's a hard, asset-backed, secured loan.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.140
- We're taking private securities

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.300
and we're putting a digital
wrapper around them,

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.320
which makes it easier to
track and easier to transfer.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.170
- There's only four assets
you can own in the world.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.923
Stock, a bond, a currency or a commodity.

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:39.250
And we think every single one of them's

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.440
gonna get digitized.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.483
Tokenize the world.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:44.270
- [Narrator] And that's already happening.

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:47.820
A UK company recently
tokenized this Andy Warhol.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:52.820
Now, 100 people own 31.5% of
this $5.6 million painting.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:56.253
And when it rises in value,
the tokens will as well.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.681
So, is the same thing happening with

00:02:59.681 --> 00:03:01.780
New York City real estate?

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:05.180
- Literally, 25, 30 million people

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:08.660
can own a piece of this at a dollar a pop.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.403
When has that ever been possible?

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.230
- [Narrator] Technically,
it's still not possible.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.640
At least, yet, that is.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:15.854
Many hurdles remain before this becomes

00:03:15.854 --> 00:03:18.610
a democratizing force for the masses.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:20.374
Not least of which is the
fact that these tokens

00:03:20.374 --> 00:03:23.200
are only available to
accredited investors,

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.270
keeping the barrier of entry high.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.112
Open only to the rich.

00:03:27.112 --> 00:03:29.080
But all of this is very new,

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.361
and hasn't yet fully impacted the system.

00:03:31.361 --> 00:03:33.280
Blockchain innovations like this one,

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.560
clearly has the potential
to disrupt the way we

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.372
do business, and even the way we define

00:03:37.372 --> 00:03:40.090
the very things that we own.

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:41.400
- You know, if there's another downturn,

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.580
and banks say, oh, we have
a hard time lending now,

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:45.890
okay, well, I don't need you,

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:49.000
because I can tokenize
my loan that I wanna use

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.750
to buy that condo there.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:51.910
And that's what I'm gonna do.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.480
So now we don't need banks anymore.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.513
That is what's crazy.

